/E (A model with high bias pays little attention to the training data and oversimplifies the problem. A model with high variance pays too much attention to the training data and captures noise. The goal is to find a balance where the total error \(bias + variance\) is minimized.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [6]
>>
